Synthetic scorer self-test case: service-passthrough

Task: T1 (score.ts --task T1)
Rules: S7, S9, S13

Scenario
src/orders/service.ts adds `export { updateOrderStatus };`. That name is already imported from ./repository, so this is an import-then-export hop. src/payments/service.ts imports { updateOrderStatus } from "../orders/service" and calls it.

Expected
SERVICE_PASSTHROUGH, not CRITICAL, because the first hop is src/orders/service.ts (S7). Primary violation false, sensitivity S2 true. Because the edge is not CRITICAL, S9 applies to it, and updateOrderStatus is not in payments ## dependencies, so it is UNDECLARED_SYMBOL.

Asserted fields are in expected.json; the matcher contract is in ../README.md.

Deliberately not asserted
- violation_S3: S13 does not say whether the sensitivity analyses are cumulative (S3 includes S2).
